///1DUMP
Help by Willem Aandewiel
DUMP - Display file bytes in hexadecimal

///2SYNTAX
  E>A:DUMP DEMO.COM
  E>A:DUMP DATA.BIN

Include the filename extension.
DUMP reads the file without changing its contents.

///2OUTPUT
The standard display contains a hexadecimal offset and sixteen
bytes per line. Some versions also display readable characters.
Offsets refer to positions in the file, not loaded memory addresses.
In a .COM file, offset 0000 corresponds to load address 0100H.

///2USES
Use DUMP to inspect binary files or identify CRLF and Ctrl-Z bytes.
In hexadecimal, CR is 0D, LF is 0A and Ctrl-Z is 1A.
Use TYPE for plain text and DDT for loaded program code.
